The issue templates are GitHub forms rather than markdown so the command and the OS and Python version are required fields, and the secrets warning sits above every field instead of in a comment people delete. The commit says 'Part of #30', not 'Closes', because the signed v0.1.0 tag must point at main after this merges, so the issue stays open for the release. CONTRIBUTING asks contributors not to squash or rebase a branch in a PR: main uses merge commits so the git notes stay on commits that end up on main.
